8001-70dac90e-26e5-4652-a022-7ac3218719ef"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3f9e40b722e0b9e6a86f935c5df77b5cfb50d56f0f5bf1b28673f5e0d992cb0a","event_uuid":"eeebbb3f-eafe-4291-872a-8700c55b55ee","position":{"commit_sha":"d4c15342000e1b81493da8f4eded7935a9ad778c","position":"1787085684377137001-eeebbb3f-eafe-4291-872a-8700c55b55ee"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ec578a310947674b49e38d9f51a5db982d42eec164f2679d65e0cd182897e551","event_uuid":"9189281c-be6f-47de-ad5d-208e8003b229","position":{"commit_sha":"0c73aa54a6982e0a78dc81333f5e8b517d8235da","position":"1787086646590502001-9189281c-be6f-47de-ad5d-208e8003b229"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 confirmed a parsimonious root cause. FastMCP builds the tool input model from each handwritten callable signature; because transition_ticket omits force/reason/caused_by/ref and claim_ticket omits force, undeclared payload keys are discarded before adapter execution. The adapter bodies independently forward only close_class or assignee, so a signature-only change would still fail. Runtime proof in an isolated tracker: live schemas omitted every field; real registered-tool capture received only current kwargs; an equivalent FastMCP tool with declared fields received exact sentinels; MCP ref selected HEAD instead of the requested older commit; and MCP caused_by closed without an edge while the library produced one. All four discriminating probes passed and temporary instrumentation was removed; the worktree is clean. The old negative force contract was deliberate in commit 95577d1960, but the signed 2026-08-18 operator ruling on restoring-shallow-blobfish explicitly rescinds it and establishes total lib/CLI/MCP parity with absent certification as the audit signal. This is therefore a defect/incomplete adapter wiring, not an unresolved design choice. Expected repair changes only the shared MCP adapter and its contracts; no caller depends on the stale omission because undeclared inputs are currently unreachable.","timestamp":1787085392492570001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final debug report. Problem: MCP transition/claim omitted supported library write controls. Proven cause: FastMCP derives input models from the stale handwritten signatures and drops undeclared extras; the handwritten delegate calls independently omitted the same values. Proof: live-schema/capture, declared-field control, two-commit ref, and caused_by differential probes all isolated the adapter boundary. Test: the final held-out real-FastMCP oracle was RED on all five slices before repair, GREEN after repair, returned to RED when signatures were removed, and returned to RED separately when forwarding was removed. It asserts public schema and persisted outcomes, so behavior-preserving refactors do not break it. Fix: transition_ticket now exposes and forwards bool force, reason, caused_by, and optional ref; claim_ticket exposes and forwards reason-bearing optional force; tool prose records absent certification as the audit signal; force_close remains absent. Scope/safety: all callers converge on the existing library/core; no behavioral dependency on the unreachable fields, no new dependency, no weakened test, and _mcp_writes.py remains 570 lines. Focused MCP, surface, close-ref, and plan-gate matrix collected 143 tests and passed; make lint and make typecheck pass. Parity census: CLI and library already enforce the rule; MCP is fixed at the shared adapter; automated callers use the library/core and need no change; dual-direction is N/A. Sibling sweep found relation-specific unlink missing only on MCP; filed and linked airy-starchy-muntjac. Import-only source provenance, internal placeholder identity tags, generic edit fields, and the separately governed CLI-only secret override were not confirmed siblings. Original reason-required close, caused_by, ref pin/sign, and both force scenarios now succeed through the real registered MCP tools; absent force and absent required reason remain rejected.","timestamp":1787086646590502001}],"created_at":1787080887680395001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d01ba4a0-8a5f-49c0-990a-fe937eb5545a","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ba48-a88a-92bd-45d0"}],"description":"## Context\nMCP transition_ticket and claim_ticket do not expose write parameters already supported by the library and CLI. Live FastMCP schemas omit transition reason, caused_by, ref, and force, and omit claim force. Undeclared payload keys are discarded before the registered callable runs. This makes compliant reason-required closes, explicit culprit attribution, explicit completion refs, and authorized plan-gate bypass unreachable over MCP.\n\nThe signed 2026-08-18 operator ruling on restoring-shallow-blobfish rescinds the older CLI/library-only force policy: force is allowed through every surface, while the absent certified attestation remains the audit signal. Deprecated force_close stays excluded.\n\n## Proven root cause\nThe handwritten MCP callable signatures in src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py were not kept in parity with the library surface. FastMCP 1.29 derives its JSON schema and argument model from those signatures, so it drops undeclared extras. Independently, the handwritten adapter calls forward only close_class for transition and assignee for claim, so adding schema fields alone would still lose them. Later caused_by and ref capabilities also stopped at this adapter boundary.\n\nA four-case runtime probe confirmed the mechanism: live schemas omitted every reported field; capture stubs saw only close_class or assignee; an equivalent FastMCP tool with declared fields received exact sentinels; MCP ref selected HEAD instead of the requested older commit; and MCP caused_by closed without the edge while the library produced it.\n\n## Repair plan\n- Add library-compatible parameters to the registered MCP signatures: transition force bool, reason string, caused_by string, ref optional string; claim force optional reason-bearing string.\n- Forward every parameter unchanged to rebar.transition or rebar.claim.\n- Replace the rescinded no-force tool prose with the absent-attestation audit model and keep force_close explicitly unavailable.\n- Replace the stale negative surface contract with positive schema assertions.\n- Add lifecycle tests through the real registered FastMCP tools for reason-required close, caused_by, explicit ref, and both start-work force paths.\n- Keep all other transition and claim semantics in the shared library/core; add no dependency or new bypass implementation.\n\n## Test contract card\n- Trigger: call the real registered MCP tools with each newly exposed parameter.\n- Boundary: FastMCP schema and validation -> MCP adapter -> public library facade -> existing command core.\n- Postconditions: declared fields appear in input schemas; exact values reach the shared core; reason-required close persists close_reason; caused_by writes the edge; explicit ref reaches verification/signing at that commit; transition force and claim force preserve their distinct library types and bypass semantics.\n- Negative controls: absent or false/empty force preserves gating; reason-required close without reason remains rejected; deprecated force_close remains absent.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] transition_ticket exposes reason, caused_by, ref, and bool force.\n- [ ] claim_ticket exposes reason-bearing optional force.\n- [ ] Every added parameter delegates unchanged to the existing library core.\n- [ ] A reason-required bug close is reachable and persists its reason through MCP.\n- [ ] MCP caused_by produces the same culprit edge as the library.\n- [ ] MCP ref targets and signs the requested immutable commit rather than HEAD.\n- [ ] Both MCP start-work force paths preserve library semantics and audit behavior.\n- [ ] Absent force and missing required reason remain rejected as before.\n- [ ] force_close remains unavailable over MCP.\n- [ ] MCP tool prose describes absent certification as the audit signal.\n- [ ] Focused tests pass.\n- [ ] make lint passes.\n- [ ] make typecheck passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"expose and forward transition and claim parameters with corrected tool contracts"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_surface.py","reason":"replace rescinded negative force contract with positive schema parity assertions"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py","reason":"exercise real FastMCP write behavior for reason, caused_by, ref, and force"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"578b758e-d26b-434f-a203-459cade875d0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1128-505b-54ac-497f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP transition_ticket/claim_ticket lack reason/caused_by/ref/force parity with CLI/lib","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["dfcf6c5d-db46-45ae-b84c-bacc13d44f57","d01ba4a0-8a5f-49c0-990a-fe937eb5545a","0937daea-7f09-4ebf-8950-fdf6adf9a1eb","578b758e-d26b-434f-a203-459cade875d0","b72a920d-d1e5-4f91-b48b-b2bc60e5d748","c02473ce-d1ac-4219-bf0f-a4bba00ec98c","fcaa44d0-af3d-4b60-824e-6db7c7adb095","85bec42d-930c-4e41-bf39-a47d41161108","96f87401-39f0-4fff-987e-184874fd0484","3a767ef4-557d-47b0-bf72-d625418b6369","70dac90e-26e5-4652-a022-7ac3218719ef","eeebbb3f-eafe-4291-872a-8700c55b55ee","9189281c-be6f-47de-ad5d-208e8003b229"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787089242526432001,"uuid":"f70f2af9-fc7e-46bc-80e4-e1585fc0dc00"}